---
/* Component — ContainerGrid
 * A responsive grid that reflows its column count to fit the space available.
 *
 * The consumer never states a column count. The grid states a minimum column
 * width and auto-fill decides how many fit — four across on a wide screen, two
 * on a tablet, one on a phone — so it adapts with no media query, and stays
 * compliant with the no-conditionals rule for free.
 *
 * No props. --bravoixr-container-column-min is currently the only token that
 * fits the role, so a prop selecting among tokens would offer exactly one
 * option. Add it when a second column size genuinely exists.
 *
 * No overflow handling either: auto-fill has no cap, so every child gets a cell
 * and there is nothing to hide.
 *
 * No block-size, matching ContainerStack — height is the ancestor's
 * responsibility. */
---

<div>
  <slot />
</div>

<style>
  div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(var(--bravoixr-container-column-min), 1fr));
    gap: var(--bravoixr-spacing-5);
  }
</style>
